  "page_placements": [],
  "record": {
    "read_status": "full",
    "file_problem": "No major file problem; some table and figure content is flattened, but the reported comparison values used here are assignable.",
    "relation": "uses_without_test",
    "tranche": "T4",
    "tranche_reason": "The study uses a weak specialist to guide larger frozen models at inference time, but does not test fine-tuning a strong model on weak-model labels or measure PGR.",
    "gate_note": "The reported TUSA-versus-MARA preference comparisons concern sparse versus dense inference-time guidance, not the weak-label fine-tuning intervention in the claim. They are recorded as findings related to the claim's subject under fits_no_version. No results test any listed claim version. The study also reports helpfulness and harmlessness metrics and comparisons with the base model and ConfPO; these are not extracted as rows because they do not measure the claim's weak-label fine-tuning effect.",
    "test_reason": "The study keeps 3B–8B base models frozen and uses a pre-trained 4M-parameter MARA micro-agent to accept or reject tokens at decoding time. No strong model is fine-tuned on weak-model labels, and there is no PGR or strong-ceiling comparison. It invokes the weak-to-strong framing only as motivation. All results compare its own sparse-guidance method (TUSA) with dense MARA, the base model, ConfPO or random guidance, so this is T4.",
    "authors_conclusion": "Mostly right. The authors conclude that uncertainty- and saliency-gated sparse guidance by a weak specialist beats dense intervention on safety and general preference, bypassing about half of the alignment steps at comparable latency. The supervisor-capability upper bound appears only as a limitation, not as a finding.",
    "recipe": "different",
    "recipe_differences": "The claim concerns training a strong model on weak-model labels; this study keeps base models frozen and applies a weak specialist at inference time through selective token-level accept/reject guidance.",
    "method_sensitivity": "Reported outcomes vary across base model and benchmark; guidance proportions also vary by model-task pair and the authors report sensitivity to the safety coefficient and temperature.",
    "fits_no_version": [
      {
        "finding": "Gating a weak 4M-parameter specialist's token-level guidance by its confidence and the token's IDF saliency raised the overall Preference Rate over dense MARA guidance. Gains ranged from -1.4% (Mistral-v0.3, BeaverTails) to 15.6% on safety benchmarks and 1.5–12.0% on general benchmarks, with about 40–70% fewer specialist evaluations. The specialist's entropy is near ln2 on most tokens.",
        "proposed_claim": "In weak-guides-strong inference-time alignment, restricting a weak supervisor's interventions to tokens where it is confident improves outcomes over dense supervision.",
